// & Shinki) keeps its Japanese, because folding it would leave a title that says nothing —
// removing a name is worse than an awkward one (client's call, 2026-09-07). The
// decomposition below drops a combining mark ONLY when it sits on an ASCII letter, so
// Cyrillic й and Greek ά come through whole while é does not.
